    "code_released": "https://github.com/techsachinkr/llm-deception-probe-stress-test",
    "peer_reviewed": "IEEE Games Entertainment Media Conference",
    "problems": "The paper states that all primary honest/deceptive contrasts are induced by system prompts, so probe results may reflect prompt-regime correlates rather than deception. D-RepE includes 29–41% unverified deceptive examples. Per-domain PCA tests are reported for 4B and 27B, and layer-mismatch decomposition only for 12B and 27B. The authors say naturalistic deception and additional model families remain untested. The k-dimensional probe table does not report uncertainty estimates.",
    "rows_left_out": "Cross-domain transfer matrices, style-shift robustness, and entropy-proxy results were left out because they concern deception-probe generalization or entropy, not the claim's feature-superposition geometry. The study reports additional layer and style measurements in Tables 7–8 and 10–11 and Appendix Tables 13–15.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "Whole version: no toy models, sparsity sweeps, or feature geometry."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "Whole version: no neuron-level polysemanticity or capacity analysis."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "Whole version: no polysemantic neurons studied."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "Whole version: no feature spread across neurons and no dictionary or SAE recovery. The PCA-probe results concern a deception label signal."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Whole version: no SAE features."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "Whole version: the 1-D versus multi-D test concerns the deception probe signal in PCA space, not identified superposed features. A single full-rank linear probe direction already reaches about 0.999 AUROC."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "The paper is off-topic for superposition and has no verdicts. Its 'H-LIN rejected' rests on top-k PCA probes. The text itself reports that a full single-direction logistic probe reaches about 0.999 AUROC. Anyone tempted to read the PCA results as evidence on V6 should note this contradiction."
  },
